def orow(p, r, verdict, prose): SO[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

orow(76, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT EAT THE LIFE WITH THE FLESH" (12:23) — THE LIMB FROM THE LIVING; IS IT NOT A REASONING: MEAT IN MILK, PERMITTED TO NOAH\'S SONS, IS FORBIDDEN TO ISRAEL — THE LIMB FROM THE LIVING, FORBIDDEN TO NOAH\'S SONS, SURELY? THE BEAUTIFUL CAPTIVE (21:11) AND HER LIKE PROVE OTHERWISE — FORBIDDEN TO NOAH\'S SONS AND PERMITTED TO ISRAEL; SO THE TEACHING SAYS IT. The row on 12:23 ({SP_(76, 5, "יפת", "תאר", "וכל", "הדומים", "לה", "תוכיח")} "the beautiful captive and all like her prove it"): THE CAPTIVE WOMAN AS A LOGIC\'S COUNTEREXAMPLE — permitted to Israel, forbidden to the nations (Sanhedrin 59a\'s Noahide list, not opened) — 21:11\'s law cited at chapter 12 for its shape. REREAD WHOLE (chapter 12, deu_12_reeh).')
orow(80, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU DISPOSSESS THEM AND DWELL IN THEIR LAND" (12:29) — SINCE IT SAYS "AND DWELL IN THEIR CITIES AND HOUSES" (19:1), MIGHT YOU NOT ADD TO THE BUILDING? "DWELL IN THEIR LAND" — WHEREVER YOU WISH TO BUILD, BUILD. ({SP_(80, 3, "כל", "מקום", "שאתה", "רוצה", "לבנות", "בנה")} "wherever you wish to build, build"): 179:2\'s twin from the other verse — the two rows one teaching. REREAD WHOLE (chapter 12, deu_12_reeh).')
orow(121, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'IF HE SAID IT WITHIN THE SIX AND NOT AT THE END OF THE SIX — HE IS NOT PIERCED, "I WILL NOT GO OUT FREE" (EXODUS 21:5) — UNTIL HE SAYS IT AT THE HOUR OF GOING OUT; SAID IT AT THE END AND NOT WITHIN — NOT PIERCED, "IF THE SLAVE SAYS" — WHILE HE IS A SLAVE. The row on 15:16 ({SP_(121, 2, "הרי", "זה", "אין", "נרצע")} "this one is not pierced"): the English\'s citation "Dt.21:5" is the EXPORT\'S ERROR for Exodus 21:5 (the Hebrew cites Exodus) — the row cites chapter 21 only by that slip; the slave\'s two declarations no bearing on 19-21. REREAD WHOLE (chapter 15, deu_15_reeh).')
orow(148, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN THERE IS FOUND" (17:2) — BY WITNESSES; SINCE IT SAYS "BY THE MOUTH OF TWO WITNESSES OR THREE A MATTER STANDS" (19:15), THIS IS A BINYAN AV (A FATHER-CASE): WHEREVER "FOUND" IS SAID, BY TWO OR THREE WITNESSES. ({SP_(148, 1, "זה", "בנין", "אב")} "this is a binyan av (a father-case)"; {SP_(148, 1, "בשני", "עדים", "ובשלשה", "עדים")} "by two witnesses and by three witnesses"): 19:15 THE FATHER-CASE of every "found" — the evidence rule\'s reach into 17:2 (and 21:1\'s "found" a slain one? the Sifrei does not say so) — the compile\'s witness parameter shared. REREAD WHOLE (chapters 17-18, deu_17_18_shoftim).')
orow(152, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"DISPUTES" (17:8) — THIS IS THE SOTAH\'S DRINKING, THE HEIFER\'S NECK-BREAKING AND THE LEPER\'S CLEANSING. ({SP_(152, 9, "ועריפת", "עגלה")} "and the heifer\'s neck-breaking"): THE HEIFER\'S RITE AMONG THE HIGH COURT\'S "DISPUTES" — the Sanhedrin\'s share in 21:1-9 (Sotah 9:1 — the measuring by the great court: the compile\'s actor) — the same three at 351:1. REREAD WHOLE (chapters 17-18, deu_17_18_shoftim).')
orow(251, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT SEEK THEIR PEACE AND THEIR GOOD" (23:7) — SINCE IT SAYS "WHEN YOU DRAW NEAR TO A CITY … CALL TO IT FOR PEACE" (20:10), MIGHT IT BE SO HERE TOO? THE TEACHING SAYS "YOU SHALL NOT SEEK THEIR PEACE". ({SP_(251, 1, "יכול", "אף", "כאן", "כן")} "might it be so here too?"): THE PEACE CALL DENIED TO AMMON AND MOAB — 20:10\'s law with an exception ahead (23:7 — the compile\'s parameter when chapter 23 is read: a pointer forward, no row read ahead). Fresh.')
orow(259, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN ONE OF YOUR GATES" (23:17) — IN YOUR GATES AND NOT IN JERUSALEM; WHEN IT SAYS "IN ONE OF YOUR GATES" — THAT HE BE NOT EXILED FROM CITY TO CITY. ({SP_(259, 5, "בשעריך", "ולא", "בירושלם")} "in your gates and not in Jerusalem"; {SP_(259, 5, "שלא", "יהא", "גולה", "מעיר", "לעיר")} "that he be not exiled from city to city"): the escaped slave\'s dwelling in the refuge\'s own words (180:8\'s "not from city to city") — the English\'s note ties it to the rebellious son\'s trial outside Jerusalem (21:18); the citation of 21 is the English\'s only. Fresh.')
orow(293, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'R. JUDAH: "YOUR EYE SHALL NOT PITY" IS SAID HERE (25:12) AND "YOUR EYE SHALL NOT PITY" THERE (19:21): AS THERE MONEY, SO HERE MONEY. ({SP_(293, 2, "מה", "לא", "תחוס", "עינך", "האמור", "להלן", "ממון")} "as \'your eye shall not pity\' said there is money"): 190:14\'s gezerah shavah (the analogy of equal words) read from the hand\'s seat — the talion money both ways. Fresh.')
orow(306, 23, 'CONTEXT', f'ANOTHER WORD: "MY DOCTRINE SHALL DROP (YAAROF) AS THE RAIN" (32:2) — R. ELIEZER SON OF R. YOSE THE GALILEAN: YAAROF IS ONLY A WORD OF KILLING, "AND BREAK THE HEIFER\'S NECK (ARFU) THERE IN THE VALLEY" (21:4); FOR WHAT DOES THE HEIFER ATONE? FOR BLOODSHED — SO WORDS OF TORAH ATONE FOR ALL TRANSGRESSIONS. ({SP_(306, 23, "אין", "יערף", "אלא", "לשון", "הריגה")} "yaarof is only a word of killing"; {SP_(306, 23, "על", "שפיכות", "דמים")} "for bloodshed"): THE NECK-BREAKING ROOT\'S HOMOGRAPH at the Song (the measure\'s eight seats) — the heifer\'s atonement "for bloodshed" named; no rule for 21. Fresh.')
orow(306, 27, 'CONTEXT', f'ANOTHER WORD: "MY DOCTRINE SHALL DROP AS THE RAIN" — R. BENAIAH: IF YOU DID WORDS OF TORAH FOR THEIR OWN SAKE THEY ARE LIFE TO YOU (PROVERBS 4:22); IF NOT, THEY KILL YOU — "YAAROF" IS ONLY KILLING, "AND BREAK THE HEIFER\'S NECK" (21:4), AND "MANY SLAIN SHE HAS FELLED" (PROVERBS 7:26). ({SP_(306, 27, "ואין", "עריפה", "אלא", "לשון", "הריגה")} "and arifah (neck-breaking) is only a word of killing"): the same homograph a second time; the "slain" (chalalim) of Proverbs 7:26 the heifer\'s word (21:1). Fresh.')
orow(351, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"THEY SHALL TEACH YOUR JUDGMENTS TO JACOB" (33:10) — THIS TEACHES THAT ALL RULINGS GO OUT ONLY FROM THEIR MOUTH, "AND BY THEIR MOUTH SHALL BE EVERY DISPUTE AND EVERY STROKE" (21:5): "DISPUTE" — THE DISPUTES OF THE HEIFER (THE RED), THE HEIFER (THE BROKEN-NECKED) AND THE SOTAH; "STROKE" — THE STROKES OF MEN, GARMENTS AND HOUSES. ({SP_(351, 1, "ריבי", "פרה", "וריבי", "עגלה", "וריבי", "סוטה")} "the disputes of the red heifer, the broken-necked heifer and the sotah"; {SP_(351, 1, "נגעי", "אדם", "ונגעי", "בגדים", "ונגעי", "בתים")} "the strokes of men, garments and houses"): 21:5\'S "EVERY DISPUTE AND EVERY STROKE" DEFINED — the three rites and the three leprosies the priests\' (208:1-4 ahead the spine\'s own reading) — the compile\'s priests\' role in the heifer\'s rite. Fresh.')
